WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.712
Unit 3 follows one G M
S A through the steps.

2
00:00:03.712 --> 00:00:07.929
It's requested, and once SailPoint
approves it, Chapter 12 checks every

3
00:00:07.929 --> 00:00:11.975
field of the approved request before
anything is created: that's S1.

4
00:00:11.975 --> 00:00:16.400
It's decided, with the guide's decision
path giving the target, in S2.

5
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.988
SailPoint approves it, and ServiceNow
opens the change record, in S3.

6
00:00:20.988 --> 00:00:25.282
The pipeline creates it from
the approved plan, in the O U,

7
00:00:25.282 --> 00:00:29.763
A E S two fifty-six, thirty days
and its retriever group, in S4.

8
00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:33.975
It's installed on the hosts and
restricted with Group Policy, in S5.

9
00:00:33.975 --> 00:00:35.834
SailPoint aggregates it,

10
00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:40.438
and the ServiceNow task closes only
on Chapter 12's re-read, in S6.

11
00:00:40.438 --> 00:00:46.250
It's watched with Defender for Identity,
in S7, and certified by its owners, in S8.

12
00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.112
It's handed over when
an owner leaves, in S9.

13
00:00:49.112 --> 00:00:53.144
And it's retired, in S10: the
pipeline disables it and moves it,

14
00:00:53.144 --> 00:00:57.999
and after ninety days with no sign-in,
a person uninstalls and deletes it.

15
00:00:57.999 --> 00:01:01.420
S11 is the move to Entra,
when the workload moves.
